# Layouts and Responsive Design

Purpose: single source of truth for screen breakpoints, shell behavior, and content width.

## Breakpoints

| Token | Width range | Target layout |
|---|---:|---|
| `xs` | `< 360` | extra-small mobile, one column |
| `sm` | `360–599` | mobile, one column |
| `md` | `600–839` | large mobile / small tablet |
| `lg` | `840–1199` | tablet / small desktop, rail or compact shell |
| `xl` | `1200–1599` | desktop: menu bar, side nav, centered content |
| `xxl` | `≥ 1600` | large desktop, max-width layouts |

## Mandatory rules

- Use centralized responsive utilities (`LayoutBuilder`, `MediaQuery.sizeOf`, or shared helpers in `lib/core/responsive/`).
- Do not duplicate screens per size unless the interaction model truly changes.
- Scale from one-column to multi-column layouts.
- Use readable max widths on large screens.
- Avoid fixed widths except intentional min/max constraints.
- Make scroll behavior explicit on small screens and content-heavy pages.
- Touch targets practical on mobile; pointer targets comfortable on desktop/web.
- Icons/buttons per [`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc).

## Navigation by width

| Width | Behavior |
|---|---|
| `< 600` | App bar plus bottom navigation or drawer |
| `600–1199` | Navigation rail or compact side navigation |
| `≥ 1200` | Menu bar and side navigation; may start collapsed |

## Desktop shell

- Top menu bar when multiple app-level actions exist.
- Side navigation for primary destinations with expanded/collapsed states.
- Collapsed width: `64–80`; expanded: `220–280`.
- Persist collapsed state as non-sensitive preference only.

## Max content widths

| Content type | Max width |
|---|---:|
| Authentication forms | `420–520` |
| General forms | `560–720` |
| Reading/detail pages | `840–1040` |
| Dashboards | `1200–1440` |
| Data-heavy pages | `1440` (+ horizontal scroll when needed) |

## Required starter files

| File | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| `lib/core/responsive/app_breakpoints.dart` | Breakpoints and helpers |
| `lib/shared/layout/responsive_shell_scaffold.dart` | Shell; public API `ResponsiveAppShell` |
